In my 听 lectures, I call Jonson’s “one peculiar quality” the blind
反. A享ed in Chapter Eleven, ì intensifies · comic
character â 备 反. This fixation holds 业o
tightly in its grip he cannot deviate from it. All aspects に identity are
bound to it; without it, he is no longer comic. What’立, this 反
